# Screenshot capture for the project cards.
#
# Primary: a GitHub repository secret of the same name, read by
# .github/workflows/screenshots.yml — a weekly (and on-demand) capture that
# opens a pull request when an image changed, so captures are reviewed and
# land in public/images/.
#
# Fallback: also set in the Vercel project's environment variables, where
# vite.config.ts recaptures into dist/ on PRODUCTION builds only (previews
# skip it). Set SCREENSHOT_AT_BUILD=off on Vercel to disable that fallback.
# Unset everywhere, the committed images ship — stale, never a failed build.
#
# It is no longer read at runtime. A Vercel Edge Function (api/screenshot.ts)
# used to hold this key and proxy captures on request, but nothing in the app
# ever called it: it was an unauthenticated public endpoint spending a metered
# quota for a feature that had already moved to static assets. Removed.
#
# Copy to .env for local use and fill in your own key — never commit the real value.
# Refresh the committed fallbacks with: npm run update-screenshots
SCREENSHOT_API_KEY=your_key_here


# ── AI mode (api/ask.ts) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Read at RUNTIME by the edge function only. These must NEVER be prefixed
# VITE_ — that prefix inlines the value into the client bundle and hands every
# visitor a key they can spend. The whole reason api/ask.ts exists is to keep
# these server-side.
#
# Set them in the Vercel project's Environment Variables dashboard.
#
# Both are OPTIONAL. With neither set, the `ai` command still works: the
# endpoint reports itself unconfigured and the terminal answers with a keyword
# match over the site's own data. A supported mode, not a broken one.
#
# Gemini is tried first, Groq second, so a rate-limited or briefly failing
# primary degrades answer quality rather than removing the feature.
#   Gemini key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#   Groq key:   https://console.groq.com/keys   (~14,400 req/day free, no card)
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Optional model overrides. Leave blank unless you mean it — pointing one at
# another provider's model id 404s every call while the key looks valid.
# Defaults: gemini-flash-lite-latest and openai/gpt-oss-120b. The `-latest`
# alias moves when Google ships a new model — pin a versioned id here if you
# want answers to stop changing underneath you.
# (llama-3.3-70b-versatile, the old Groq default, was retired on 2026-08-16.)
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-flash-lite-latest
# Tried when the primary Gemini model is overloaded or failing, before Groq.
# GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# Optional shared store for Ask AI (Upstash Redis, or Vercel KV which is the
# same thing). Without it, rate limits, the daily budget and cached answers are
# per edge instance — best-effort. With it, they hold across every instance.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
# (KV_REST_API_URL / KV_REST_API_TOKEN are read too, as Vercel KV names them.)

# Opening questions are answered once per deploy and replayed. Set to `off`
# to always ask the model (useful while editing the prompt).
# ASK_ANSWER_CACHE=off

# `npm run eval:ai` asks the real model a fixed set of questions and checks the
# answers are grounded. It reads the keys above; it is never part of `npm test`.
